<section id="ch7" class="chapter">
  <div class="ch-num">Chapter 7</div>
  <h2>Foundations of Intelligence: Knowledge as Lack of Ignorance, Observation Fibers, Abstraction, Self-Reference, and Meaning</h2>

  <p>If statistical next-token sampling and scalar preference fitting fail by construction, what is the positive mathematical theory of intelligence? This chapter unifies the formal epistemology developed across <code>lib/observation.hypercubical</code>, <code>lib/fiber.hypercubical</code>, <code>lib/obs.hypercubical</code>, <code>lib/meaning.hypercubical</code>, <code>lib/singularity.hypercubical</code>, <a href="/knowledge-is-a-lack-of-ignorance"><em>Knowledge Is a Lack of Ignorance</em></a>, <a href="/lawvere-fixed-points"><em>Lawvere's Fixed-Point Theorem</em></a>, <a href="/language-is-trained-synesthesia"><em>Language Is Trained Synesthesia</em></a>, and <code>docs/to-francois-chollet.hypercubical</code>.</p>

  <h3 id="sec-7-1">7.1 Knowledge as Lack of Ignorance and Cubical Observation Fibers</h3>
  <p>Both classical Greek epistemology (<em>a-lētheia</em>, un-concealment; Plato's <em>Meno</em>, <em>Phaedo</em>, <em>Theaetetus</em>) and classical Indian epistemology (<em>avidyā</em>, ignorance as an obscuration veiling an intrinsically knowing faculty; <em>Muṇḍaka Upaniṣad</em>, Umāsvāti's <em>Tattvārtha Sūtra</em>) define knowledge negatively as the <strong>removal of ignorance</strong>. Rather than accumulating unverified point estimates, knowing eliminates world-histories incompatible with observation. In cubical type theory (<code>lib/observation.hypercubical</code>, <code>lib/fiber.hypercubical</code>), this becomes an exact structural decomposition.</p>
  <p>Let $H : \mathrm{Type}$ be the space of world histories and $o : H \to O$ an observation map yielding the reading $y = o(h) \in O$ accessible to an agent. By <code>fiberEquiv</code> in <code>lib/fiber.hypercubical</code>, the entire space of histories decomposes without loss into the disjoint dependent sum of its <strong>observation fibers</strong>:</p>
  <div class="eq-box">$$\mathrm{Fib}_o(y) \;:\equiv\; \sum_{h : H} \big(o(h) \equiv y\big), \qquad H \;\simeq\; \sum_{y : O} \mathrm{Fib}_o(y).$$</div>
  <p>A reading $y$ <strong>warrants</strong> a proposition $P : H \to \mathrm{Type}$ if and only if $P$ holds across <em>every</em> history compatible with $y$ (<code>Warrants</code> in <code>lib/observation.hypercubical</code>):</p>
  <div class="eq-box">$$\mathrm{Warrants}(o, y, P) \;:\equiv\; \prod_{hp : \mathrm{Fib}_o(y)} P(\mathrm{fst}\,hp).$$</div>
  <p>Four machine-checked constructions in <code>lib/observation.hypercubical</code> govern all rational epistemology:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Monotonicity under refinement (<code>warrants-refine</code>):</strong> If a finer observation $o' : H \to O'$ factors $o = g \circ o'$, then $\mathrm{Warrants}(g \circ o', g(y'), P) \to \mathrm{Warrants}(o', y', P)$. Acquiring new evidence strictly shrinks the compatible fiber without ever fabricating a point inside it.</li>
    <li><strong>No autonomous law on partial projections (<code>no-observed-law</code>):</strong> Consider the deterministic, reversible two-bit universe $J = \mathrm{Bool} \times \mathrm{Bool}$ evolving by the involution <code>whole-step</code> $(a, b) \mapsto (a \oplus b, b)$ (<code>whole-step-involution</code>), observed solely through its first coordinate $\mathrm{fst}$. Then <code>no-observed-law</code> constructs a direct proof of <code>Empty</code> ($\bot$) from any purported closed transition map $g : \mathrm{Bool} \to \mathrm{Bool}$ satisfying $\forall j.\; g(\mathrm{fst}\,j) \equiv \mathrm{fst}(\mathrm{whole\text{-}step}\,j)$: at $(\mathrm{true}, \mathrm{false})$ it forces $g(\mathrm{true}) \equiv \mathrm{true}$, while at $(\mathrm{true}, \mathrm{true})$ it forces $g(\mathrm{true}) \equiv \mathrm{false}$, contradicting <code>true≢false</code>. What looks like irreducible "Bayes noise" on an observed coordinate is structurally the fiber of unobserved coupled state — explaining why passive observational predictors hit an irreducible ceiling that active observation dissolves.</li>
    <li><strong>Relational reception (<code>readings</code>):</strong> A participant's reception relation $\mathrm{Receive} : S \to M \to S \to A \to \mathrm{Type}$ relates current state $s$, received utterance $u \in M$, next state $s'$, and interpreted act $a \in A$, giving the fiber of compatible readings $\sum_{s':S}\sum_{a:A} \mathrm{Receive}(s, u, s', a)$ — directly formalizing communicative ambiguity without premature collapse.</li>
    <li><strong>Contractibility of singletons (<code>sing-contr</code>):</strong> $\mathrm{Sing}(a) \equiv \sum_{x:A} (a \equiv x)$ is contractible (<code>isContr</code>). Attaching an equality proof to a known value adds zero spurious degrees of freedom; when an observation fiber contracts to a singleton, ignorance vanishes completely.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Whenever $\mathrm{Fib}_o(y)$ admits a <strong>split witness</strong> — two compatible histories $(h_1, h_2)$ with $P(h_1)$ and $\neg P(h_2)$ — asserting $P$ is provably unwarranted. Instead of sampling a hallucinated completion, a rational agent issues an <strong>active query</strong> whose outcome separates $h_1$ from $h_2$ (unifying active learning, Settles 2009, and CIRL, Hadfield-Menell et al. 2016, inside dependent type theory).</p>

