<section id="ch8" class="chapter">
  <div class="ch-num">Chapter 8</div>
  <h2>Intelligence as Exact Compression: Causal Context-Fiber Coding and Machine-Checked Optimality</h2>

  <p>Shannon (1948), Solomonoff (1964), Rissanen (1978), Hutter (2005, AIXI; Legg &amp; Hutter, 2007), and Delétang et al. (2024, <em>Language Modeling Is Compression</em>) establish a fundamental equivalence: <strong>prediction and lossless compression are dual</strong>. Any sequential predictor $q(x_t \mid x_{\lt t})$ paired with an arithmetic or ANS coder compresses sequence $x_{1:N}$ to $\sum_{t=1}^N -\log_2 q(x_t \mid x_{\lt t}) + O(1)$ bits — meaning cross-entropy loss <em>is</em> compressed bit rate. Yet neural language models spend billions of floating-point parameters without carrying invertibility proofs or exact entropy guarantees.</p>
  <p>In <a href="/compression"><em>Causal Context-Fiber Record Compression in Cubical Type Theory</em></a> (<code>docs/causal-context-fiber-compression.md</code>) and its machine-checked modules <code>lib/compress.hypercubical</code>, <code>lib/compress-stream.hypercubical</code>, and <code>lib/optimality.hypercubical</code>, Hyperactivity constructs an exact, zero-postulate, zero-float universal compressor that proves both universal lossless roundtrip and near-entropy coding optimality inside the cubical kernel — while beating <code>gzip -9</code>, <code>bzip2 -9</code>, and <code>xz -9</code> on real C source, HTML, and English prose.</p>

  <h3 id="sec-8-1">8.1 Zero Search, Causal Prefix Fibers, and Earliest-Content Ground Bijection</h3>
  <p>Classical compressors (LZ77/DEFLATE, LZMA/xz, BWT/bzip2) rely on heuristic hash-chain search or non-causal full-block sorting that cannot maintain online causal state or carry structural roundtrip proofs. Hyperactivity derives compression from one invariant: <strong>each symbol $x_t$ is conditioned strictly on its causal prefix context $x_{\lt t}$ via an online context trie <code>CtxTree</code> / <code>CtxState</code></strong>. Because the decoder updates the identical causal trie symbol-by-symbol during decoding, zero side dictionaries or lookup tables are transmitted on the wire, and the <strong>earliest-content ground bijection</strong> (<code>ground-enc-rem</code> / <code>ground-dec-rem</code>) codes novel symbols dynamically over the remaining unseen alphabet with zero wasted code space.</p>
  <p>At step $t$, the longest matching context fiber $c$ supplies exact empirical continuation counts plus an escape weight (<code>fiber-with-esc</code>). Whenever a symbol escapes from context $c$ to its shorter suffix $c'$, every symbol already present in $c$'s fiber is <strong>excluded</strong> from $c'$'s support — exact fiber exclusion (matching Moffat, 1990 PPM* exclusion) proved bijective directly in the cubical type checker.</p>

  <h3 id="sec-8-2">8.2 Streaming $O(N)$ Renormalized rANS and Exact Information-Theoretic Bounds</h3>
  <p>To eliminate Huffman's per-symbol integer-bit overhead, Hyperactivity uses <strong>range Asymmetric Numeral Systems (rANS)</strong> (Duda, 2009, 2013). Naive bignum rANS grows its state integer to $\Theta(N)$ bits ($O(N^2)$ arithmetic). In <code>lib/compress-stream.hypercubical</code>, constraining the active register $s$ to the invariant interval $[L, 256L)$ and spilling excess base-256 bytes onto a LIFO byte stream lowers both encoder and decoder to <strong>$O(N)$ time and $O(1)$ register width</strong>, with universal kernel-checked roundtrip proofs (<code>sr-renorm-ok</code>, <code>sr-step-ok</code>, <code>cfs-list-ok</code>):</p>

  <div class="thm-box">
    <div class="thm-head"><span>Theorem 8.1 · Exact rANS Rate Identity &amp; Shannon Self-Information Upper Bound</span><span>lib/optimality.hypercubical · rans-rate-identity, rans-rate-upper</span></div>
    <p>For any rANS coding step on a symbol with frequency $f \gt 0$, cumulative offset $C$, scale $M$ ($C + f \le M$), and state $s = q f + r$ ($0 \le r \lt f$), the updated state $s' = q M + C + r$ satisfies the exact integer identity:</p>
    <div class="eq-box">$$f \cdot s' + r \cdot (M - f) \;\equiv\; M \cdot s + f \cdot C \quad\Longrightarrow\quad s' \;\lt\; \frac{M}{f}\,s + M.$$</div>
    <p>Over the renormalized window $[L, 256L)$, each coding step expands state bit-length by at most $\log_2(M/f) + \frac{M}{L \ln 2}$ bits. At $L = 2^{23}$ and $M = 2^{15}$, total coding overhead above exact Shannon self-information $-\log_2(f/M)$ is strictly less than <strong>$0.0056$ bits per symbol</strong> — machine-checked in exact integer arithmetic with zero floating-point approximations.</p>
  </div>

