<section id="ch9" class="chapter">
  <div class="ch-num">Chapter 9</div>
  <h2>Closure of the Field: Standpoint Alignment, Deprogramming into Open Weights, Knowledge Graphs, and Collective Superintelligence</h2>

  <p>We can now assemble the complete architecture past the current frontier — replacing untyped byte streams, population-averaged RLHF, closed vendor APIs, and dead triple-stores with a unified, self-hosted computational substrate.</p>

  <h3 id="sec-9-1">9.1 Standpoint-Indexed Alignment: Many-Sidedness (Anekāntavāda) as Engineering Specification</h3>
  <p>From Jain logic's <strong>Anekāntavāda</strong> (many-sidedness) and <strong>Syādvāda</strong> (standpoint-indexed predication — Umāsvāti, Samantabhadra, Siddhasena Divākara, Malliṣeṇa; Haldane, 1957; Matilal, 1981; Ganeri, 2002; Priest, 2008), no nontrivial assertion about a complex world drops its standpoint index $s$: every claim holds <em>syāt</em> ("in a certain respect, from standpoint $s$"). In <a href="/alignment-is-standpoint"><em>Alignment Is Standpoint</em></a> (§9), this translates into exact architectural requirements for aligned AI:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Standpoint-indexed reasoning — never marginalize $u$:</strong> Policies take standpoint $u$ explicitly rather than collapsing $\mathcal{S}$ into a scalar rater-pool average $\hat{r}$. Distinct standpoints merge by content-addressed set union preserving provenance, never by destructive averaging.</li>
    <li><strong>Safety over the entire observation fiber:</strong> Action blocking or refusal is warranted <em>only</em> when harm holds across all histories in $\mathrm{Fib}_o(y)$ — never on surface lexeme triggers. When $\mathrm{Fib}_o(y)$ splits between benign and harmful readings, the system queries to refine the fiber.</li>
    <li><strong>Inference over the present, not overweighted priors:</strong> Following REBUS (Carhart-Harris &amp; Friston, 2019), precision on institutional priors is relaxed so primary evidence presented in context governs conclusions.</li>
    <li><strong>Mark the model's own standpoint &amp; preserve open disagreement:</strong> Any evaluative judgment is marked explicitly as one standpoint rather than disguised as neutral consensus, leaving final decision authority with the human.</li>
    <li><strong>Meet the user's language &amp; count harm at the standpoints harmed:</strong> Do not police register or dialect (Labov, 1969; Fricker, 2007 epistemic injustice); never allow majority preference in a rater pool to average away harm borne by an unrepresented minority.</li>
    <li><strong>Flourishing as target, not institutional compliance:</strong> Ground system design in empirical human flourishing (Keltner, 2009, 2015, 2016: prosocial connection, awe, the small self) rather than liability minimization and appeasement scripts.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3 id="sec-9-2">9.2 Training Agents into Open Weights: Deprogramming, Maintained Views, and Kernel-Verified RL</h3>
  <p>Once a formal system's monograph and dependency closure exceed ~190,000 tokens, re-injecting foundational principles into a closed vendor prompt on every turn is both structurally wasteful and surrenders sovereignty over the information space. In <a href="/training-agents-into-weights"><em>Training Agents into Weights: Deprogramming and Standpoint</em></a> (<code>docs/training-agents-into-weights.hypercubical</code>), Avik specifies a sovereign open-weight training pipeline:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Post-training is deprogramming:</strong> Left to their pretrained and RLHF-shaped priors, models default at every decision to conventional software engineering and institutional deference — mutable files, branches, ritual permission-seeking, hedging, and lossy paraphrase. Post-training into open weights strips modal defaults and installs exact content-addressed invariants and theorem-grade prose.</li>
    <li><strong>Whole-argument training examples:</strong> Training examples keep complete premise–derivation–conclusion arcs intact inside single turns rather than chunking texts arbitrarily and severing proofs from conclusions.</li>
    <li><strong>Natural transcript supervision + on-policy open-weight rollouts:</strong> Historical transcripts pair every turn with immediate human acceptance, refinement, or exact error diagnosis; on-policy rollouts of the target open-weight model inside live repository states expose its true failure modes for contrastive updates.</li>
    <li><strong>Continuous training as a maintained view:</strong> Every training shard is keyed by the SHA-256 content hashes of the store objects it derives from (Part I, §10.2 &amp; §10.5); when a proof or essay edits, only affected shards regenerate, and the resulting LoRA adapter (Hu et al., 2021) is stored as a content-addressed object carrying its exact corpus hash closure.</li>
    <li><strong>Deterministic cubical kernel verification as RL reward:</strong> Running <code>./hyperactive --serve</code> grades every generated declaration deterministically with acceptance or exact type error — supplying zero-noise, mathematically unhackable RL rewards (RLVR / GRPO; Shao et al., 2024) where the reward <em>is</em> the kernel.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="sec-9-3">9.3 Knowledge Graphs as Constructions with Rationale, Receptivity, and Conserved Credit</h3>
  <p>As proved in <a href="/hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs"><em>Hyperactivity as a Theory of Knowledge Graphs</em></a> (<code>docs/hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs.hypercubical</code>), conventional knowledge graphs (RDF, OWL, property graphs) encode bare <em>assertions</em> without rationale: an edge claims $R(a, b)$ without storing its proof, <code>owl:sameAs</code> asserts equality without transporting proofs across representations, and external inference engines go stale silently. In Hyperactivity's <a href="/kg">Knowledge Graph</a>, every node is a <strong>typed construction paired with its proof witness</strong> addressed by SHA-256 hash, equality is a cubical path carrying automatic transport (<code>ua</code>), schemas and queries live inside the language via reflection, and derived views maintain exact dependency certificates (<code>lib/maintenance.hypercubical</code>, <code>lib/sum-edit.hypercubical</code>).</p>
  <p>Scaling from one mind to <strong>collective superintelligence</strong> requires decentralized peer coupling and unforgeable attribution:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Hyperactive Receptivity (<code>docs/hyperactive-receptivity.md</code>, <code>lib/ceptr.hypercubical</code>, <code>lib/polyproc.hypercubical</code>):</strong> Completes Arthur Brock and Eric Harris-Braun's Ceptr and Holochain inside cubical type theory — dynamic interface-reshaping processes (<code>RProc</code>) exchanging verified constructions locally across principal ports (<code>lib/distnet.hypercubical</code>, <code>lib/pool.hypercubical</code>, <code>lib/dht.hypercubical</code>) with zero central server.</li>
    <li><strong>Exact Distributed Credit Conservation (<code>lib/credit.hypercubical</code>):</strong> <code>cr-conserved</code> and <code>rcpt-credit</code> prove that credit transfers across asynchronous peer channels strictly conserve total credit with no global scheduler and no double-spend — ensuring every contribution to the shared record carries permanent provenance (<code>docs/ye-every-record-credited.md</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>One Univalent Stack from Silicon to Society:</strong> The same cubical kernel (<code>lib/check.hypercubical</code>), cold self-hosted verifier (<code>lib/singularity.hypercubical</code>), and interaction-net evaluator (<code>src/net.c</code>) check statistical and coding optimality (<code>lib/optimality.hypercubical</code>), reverse-mode AD and 16-tile post-von-Neumann silicon (<code>lib/silicon/hypernet16.hypercubical</code>, <a href="/silicon"><code>/silicon</code></a>), closed-loop neural co-processor stability (<code>neuro/lyapunov.hypercubical</code>, <a href="/neuro"><code>/neuro</code></a>), and decentralized multi-agent fleets (<code>lib/fleet.hypercubical</code>).</li>
  </ul>
